%li.jpost#devops
  .title.expandable
    %a.more-details
      %i.icon-plus
    %h3.name Dev Ops Engineer

  .details
    .details-container
      %p.location
        San Francisco, CA United States

      %p The Action.IO platform engineering team works on the infrastructure and tools that power our cutting-edge cloud development platform.
      %p We’re looking for talented engineers who are passionate about building fault-tolerant distributed systems, automating configuration and deployment, and bringing about a level of security to our deployment process which enables our application teams to deploy features quickly and consistently.

      %h4 Responsibilities
      %p.reqs
        %ul
          %li Implement internal tools such as monitoring, analytics and automated backup in the form of services
          %li Be responsible for the uptime of customer-facing services
          %li Design and lead infrastructure failure simulations and implement corrective measures
          %li Benchmark app performance and design scalable and performant systems and APIs

      %h4 Technologies
      %p You'll have worked with these or similar technologies:
      %p.reqs
        %ul
          %li Ruby / Python / Node.JS / Go
          %li Amazon Web Services (EC2, ELB, S3 in multiple regions)
          %li Ansible / Chef / Puppet (or configuration management system of your choice)
          %li Vagrant
          %li Message queues: Rabbitmq / Activemq / Redis
          %li Monit / Nagios / Sensu
          %li CollectD / Diamond / Riemann
          %li Graphite
          %li Logstash
          %li StatsD
          %li Git
          %li Nginx / HAProxy
          %li PostgreSQL

      %p.actions
        To apply, please send us the following:

        %p.reqs
          %ul
            %li Resume
            %li Github Profile
            %li Links to side/hobby projects that you have built

      .details-actions
        %p
          = mail_to 'jobs@action.io?subject=DevOps%20Engineer', 'Apply for this Job', encode: 'javascript', class: "btn btn-success"
